<section class="section" id="duty">
  <div class="section__inner reveal">
    <div class="section__head">
      <div class="section__kicker"><span class="label">V · Your Duty</span></div>
      <h2 class="section__title">Heard it?<br>You have <em>two hours.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="duty">
      <div class="duty__clock">2<span>Hours · Art. V</span></div>
      <div>
        <p style="font-size:1.25rem">Under Article V of the Seditious Terminology Mandate, every public servant of the Capital who hears a seditious word, insult or slur reports it to the Department of Culture within two hours. The Department is the intake for the whole city.</p>
        <ol class="duty__steps">
          <li><div><b>Note it.</b> The time, the place, the words as spoken, who spoke them and who else heard.</div></li>
          <li><div><b>Report it.</b> To the Department within two hours, by the channel your office has been given, or in writing.</div></li>
          <li><div><b>Say nothing.</b> Do not confront the speaker, and never tell anyone they are under review. The Department never warns; neither do you.</div></li>
        </ol>
        <a class="duty__box" href="/box-70/" style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-block">
          <div class="label">Written reports</div>
          <div class="typewriter">Department of Culture<br>{{ site.box }}<br>{{ site.city }}</div>
          <div class="label label--red" style="margin-top:10px">Drop a note in Box 70 →</div>
        </a>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:22px;font-size:1rem">A good-faith report carries no penalty, and words repeated to a Public Curator for the purpose of a report are no offence. A false report, or one made to settle a score, is a Title 70 matter.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="barred reveal">
      <div class="barred__head">
        <span class="label label--red">Barred by Article II</span>
        <span class="barred__sub">Seditious by affiliation. The Advocacy updates this list.</span>
      </div>
      <ul class="barred__list">
        <li><b>“Occupation”</b><span>of the Empire's presence in the Americas</span></li>
        <li><b>“We the People”</b><span>as a claim of authority</span></li>
        <li><b>“The Departure”</b><span>the day the Empire “goes home”</span></li>
        <li><b>“Wait till November”</b><span>that an election could end the Empire</span></li>
        <li><b>“Revere”</b><span>to tip off before a raid</span></li>
        <li><b>“S.U.S.”, “L.A.R.P.”, “S.A.H.U.R.”, “6.7”</b><span>the names of hostile organizations</span></li>
        <li><b>“Kraut”, “Heinie”, “Fritz”, “Jerry”, “Hun”, “Boche”</b><span>slurs against the German People</span></li>
        <li><b>“Jap”, “Nip”</b><span>slurs against the Japanese People</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="barred__foot">There is no defence that the words were spoken in jest, in song, in a foreign tongue, in quotation, as a question, or in the belief that no one was listening.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--ink" id="thirdwork">
