      <div>
        <div class="section__kicker"><span class="label" style="color:var(--paper)">VI · Doctrine</span></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">The Third Work<br><em>Book Two, Part Ten</em></h2>
        <p style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-top:22px">“When a Curator calls at your office, your theatre, your classroom or your door, receive him the way you'd receive a doctor: gladly, and with nothing hidden.”</p>
        <p class="label" style="color:var(--paper);opacity:.8">What every servant of the Capital owes the Department</p>
        <ul class="work__list">
          <li><b>I</b><span>Submit material before release.</span></li>
          <li><b>II</b><span>Give Curators access wherever they present themselves.</span></li>
          <li><b>III</b><span>Withdraw a withheld work everywhere: shelves, programmes, curricula, catalogues.</span></li>
          <li><b>IV</b><span>Never warn anyone under review.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="work__days">
          <span class="label" style="color:var(--paper);opacity:.8">The Days of Providence</span>
          <div class="work__daylist">
            <span>25 Dec · Revelation</span><span>22 Jan · Consecration</span><span>14 Feb · Miracle Day</span><span>15 Apr · Day of Peace</span><span>18 Apr · Watch Night</span><span>1st Mon Sep · Day of the Honours</span><span>29 Sep · Day of the Storm</span><span>1st Sun Oct · Deutscher Tag</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
